From: AVEVA <noreply@aveva.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Install db_bench_tool as a static library so plugins can
 register a custom Env/FileSystem before invoking db_bench_tool().

The upstream RocksDB build compiles the db_bench sources directly into the
db_bench executable, which prevents downstream wrappers from calling
rocksdb::db_bench_tool() after registering a custom FileSystem plugin.

This patch installs db_bench's non-main sources as a standalone static
library `db_bench_tool`, exported via RocksDBTargets, gated only on
WITH_GFLAGS (db_bench_tool.cc compiles to a stub without GFLAGS defined).
It intentionally does NOT hook into WITH_BENCHMARK_TOOLS: that option also
builds table_reader_bench, memtablerep_bench, hash_table_bench, etc., which
pull in RocksDB's `testharness`/gtest on Windows. RocksDB's fused gtest
CMakeLists builds gtest as a shared library there but exports no symbols,
so link.exe produces no import lib (gtestd.lib), breaking those targets.
Keeping WITH_BENCHMARK_TOOLS/WITH_TOOLS OFF (as this port already does)
avoids that unrelated breakage entirely.

Downstream consumers can link `RocksDB::db_bench_tool` and call
`rocksdb::db_bench_tool(argc, argv)` from their own main.

---
 CMakeLists.txt | 21 +++++++++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 21 insertions(+)

diff --git a/CMakeLists.txt b/CMakeLists.txt
--- a/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -1625,6 +1625,27 @@
   endif()
 endif()
 
+if(WITH_GFLAGS)
+  # AVEVA: expose db_bench's guts as an installed static library so downstream
+  # wrappers can register custom FileSystem plugins before invoking
+  # rocksdb::db_bench_tool(argc, argv). Deliberately independent of
+  # WITH_BENCHMARK_TOOLS/WITH_TOOLS -- see commit message for why.
+  add_library(db_bench_tool STATIC
+    tools/simulated_hybrid_file_system.cc
+    tools/tool_hooks.cc
+    tools/db_bench_tool.cc)
+  target_link_libraries(db_bench_tool
+    PUBLIC ${ROCKSDB_LIB} ${THIRDPARTY_LIBS})
+  target_include_directories(db_bench_tool PUBLIC
+    $<BUILD_INTERFACE:${CMAKE_CURRENT_SOURCE_DIR}/include>
+    $<INSTALL_INTERFACE:${CMAKE_INSTALL_INCLUDEDIR}>)
+  install(TARGETS db_bench_tool
+    EXPORT RocksDBTargets
+    COMPONENT devel
+    ARCHIVE DESTINATION "${CMAKE_INSTALL_LIBDIR}"
+    INCLUDES DESTINATION "${CMAKE_INSTALL_INCLUDEDIR}")
+endif()
+
 if(WITH_BENCHMARK_TOOLS)
   add_executable(db_bench${ARTIFACT_SUFFIX}
     tools/simulated_hybrid_file_system.cc
